{"name":"Infectious Love","hex":"#bb1177","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"infectious","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Caused by an agent that enters the host's body (such as a bacterium, virus, parasite, or prion); often, also, transmitted among hosts via any of various routes (for example, contact, droplet-borne, airborne, waterborne, foodborne, fomite-borne, or bloodborne).","Able to infect others; capable of transmitting pathogens."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/infectious"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Infection","blocks":[{"text":"An infection is the invasion of tissues by pathogens, their multiplication, and the reaction of host tissues to the infectious agent and the toxins they produce. An infectious disease is an illness resulting from an infection, and some infectious diseases are also communicable (transmissible)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Cutaneous_abscess_MRSA_staphylococcus_aureus_7826_lores.jpg/330px-Cutaneous_abscess_MRSA_staphylococcus_aureus_7826_lores.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Infection"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Chain_of_Infection.png/500px-Chain_of_Infection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Chain_of_Infection.png/1280px-Chain_of_Infection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Chain_of_Infection.png/500px-Chain_of_Infection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chain of infection; the chain of events that lead to infection","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChain_of_Infection.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Dit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg/330px-Dit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Dit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg/330px-Dit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Infection of an ingrown toenail; there is pus (yellow) and resultant inflammation (redness and swelling around the nail).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADit_del_peu_gros_infectat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Pathogenic_Infection.png/500px-Pathogenic_Infection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Pathogenic_Infection.png/500px-Pathogenic_Infection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This image depicts the steps of pathogenic infection.[16]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APathogenic_Infection.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d7/CulexNil.jpg/500px-CulexNil.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse